{
  "id": "reversal-shift",
  "term": "reversal shift",
  "definition": "In this learning context, a reversal shift is an early change in movement strategy in which a person responds as if the required correction is the opposite direction, applying about a 180° reversal. It describes a compensatory directional adjustment used during visuomotor adaptation when the task is difficult.",
